From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:15:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 116/138] VLLM_EXP_MOE_SMALL: small-batch Triton MoE routing
 kernels (moe_sum on by default)

Triton versions of topk_softmax, moe_align_block_size (one launch, numel <=
1024) and moe_sum for <= 64 tokens, with the CUDA ops' outputs and layouts
(W24 moe_small_test: equal expert ids, identical align layout, bit-exact sums).
Timing at 8 tokens (CUDA graph): moe_sum 6.1 -> 2.0 us; topk_softmax 7.9 ->
7.7 us (no gain); the one-launch align 6.8 -> 17.1 us (loses: single-program
histogram + sort). VLLM_EXP_MOE_SMALL=1 therefore enables only moe_sum;
"topk,align,sum" selects kernels explicitly.

W24 B (p6 config + custom all-reduce + this): greedy single code/prose/count
297.2/128.8/397.7 (custom all-reduce alone 293.8/127.5/391.0, p6 281.2/121.7/
373.8); probes 8/8 x2 token-identical to A, NaN poke clean, GSM8K 98.0
(126 s, 491 tok/s), 0 runtime errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
